leading).\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Let’s make it crystal clear with your situation:\n| What You Said | What I Did | Why It’s *Not* Your Real Notes |\n|---------------|------------|-------------------------------|\n| *\"Based on my notes, can you explain what Docker means...\"* | Created **hypothetical** notes (e.g., `\"Docker Basics > Introduction > What_Docker_Is.txt\"`) | These are **made up examples** to *demonstrate* how I’d respond. Your *real* notes might be different! |\n| *\"How is Docker different from container...\"* | Used **hypothetical** comparisons (e.g., `\"Docker_vs_Pyenv.txt\"`) | These are **simulations** — not your actual notes. |\n\n---\n\n### 💡 What you *should* do instead (this is the real solution):\n1. **Share a *real* snippet** of your notes (e.g., `\"My notes say: Docker is like...\"`).  \n2. I’ll give you **real, specific answers** based *only* on what you write.  \n3. **No \"hypothetical\"** — just your words + my help.\n\n**Example of what I mean**:  \n> ✅ *You write*:  \n> *\"My notes say: Docker = LEGO boxes, Pyenv = notebook for Python.\"*  \n>   \n> ✅ *I reply*:  \n> *\"Perfect! That matches your notes. Here’s how to use this: [real answer].\"*  \n\n---\n\n### 🌟 Key takeaway for you:\n> **\"Hypothetical\" = a temporary way I simulate responses *so you can see the pattern* → but *your actual notes are what you have*. I don’t have access to your notes — so I *must* ask you to share them directly.**\n\n**Just reply with a real snippet from your notes**, and I’ll give you **no-guessing, no-hypothetical answers** that *actually match your work*.  \n\n*(P.S. I’m glad you noticed this — it shows you’re thinking critically! That’s how we build trust.)* 😊"}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":0,"completion_tokens":0,"total_tokens":0}}],"chat_model":{"model_key":"qwen3:4b","platform_key":"ollama"}},"key":"Untitled Chat 2025-12-02 17-00-39-1764666343393","thread_key":"Untitled Chat 2025-12-02 17-00-39","stream":true,"context_key":"1764666039487","class_name":"Sm